      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would you mind naming these `symbols_node` and `symbols_node_mut`?\n\nWhat I had in mind was\n```\n    pub fn symbols(\u0026self) -\u003e Result\u003cPropertyIterator\u003e {\n        if let Some(node) \u003d self.node(cstr!(\"/__symbols__\"))? {\n            node.properties()\n        } else {\n            Ok(PropertyIterator::empty())\n        }\n```\n(and the same for `.aliases()`) making client code super readable with\n```\nfor (symbol, path) in fdt.symbols()? {\n```\nbut as this syntax anyway requires introducing an iterator that provides the tuple, let\u0027s not do it now but later as a clean-up. Still, let\u0027s reserve the `.symbols()` name for it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 979,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 979,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "f163d7629a9e9535b5a339492acdb13738991ec2",
