      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let me keep it as-is.\n\nI don\u0027t understand what\u0027s your expectation of `libfdt/src/lib.rs`. Previously you mentioned that it\u0027s a thin layer for FFI calls, but now you\u0027re proposing to add helper method(s) specifically for `pvmfw` specific use cases. I thought that this is for FFI adaptor to provide Rust style interfaces, but we\u0027re adding more and more.\nCould you share me your opinion about what\u0027s allowed here? How to classify a new API between here and `vmbase/fdt.rs`?\n\n\nMy random thoughts: (you don\u0027t need to answer)\n  - If we add `symbols()` and `symbols_node()`, then why don\u0027t we rename `root()` to `root_node()`, and `memory()` to `memory_reg()`? Naming doesn\u0027t seem to be consistent, especially if we add both `symbols()` and `symbols_node()`\n  - I think that `for (symbol, path) in fdt.symbols()` is shorter and clean because iterator hides `Result` for getting `name` and `value`.\n  - `for (symbol, path) in fdt.symbols()` sounds like that you\u0027re expecting to add another iterator that returns tuple of `(\u0026CStr, \u0026CStr)`. However, such API isn\u0027t defined in `DTC`\u0027s `libfdt` and `libfdt/src/lib.rs` is more diverge. Would such iterator worth to add it? The one liner can be implemented with existing APIs with +3 lines. It can be acceptable.",
